# Colorectal Cancer Screening Cognitive Support
library "CRC Recommendation".

// CRL representation of the demo-content-r4 colorectal cancer screening
// COGNITIVE SUPPORT example. Used for round-trip validation:
//
//   CRL author writes this file
//     → CRL→FHIR-def emit pipeline (Todo 1+2+3)
//     → produces FHIR resources
//     → compared to expected-fhir/ (copied from demo-content-r4)
//
// Round-trip test confirms emit shape matches the IG reference example
// in terms of resource set, profile claims, type codings, action
// nesting, and cross-resource canonical references.
//
// The Prior Authorization (PA) flavor of the cc-screening corpus is
// intentionally NOT modeled here — operator scope: cognitive support
// first, PA in a future fixture.
//
// Concept names are clinical-narrative phrasing chosen to be readable
// in the emitted action.title/description and the action.condition
// CQL identifier. The actual CQL implementation of these concepts
// lives in the existing demo-content-r4 ColorectalCancerCaseFeatures
// library (see ../expected-fhir/library/).

// ============ Concepts ============
// One concept per condition referenced in the decision tree.
// These are CaseFeature-style booleans on patient state — typed
// as Observation since the IG models them as Observation
// CaseFeatures (see ColorectalCancerCaseFeatures.json).

// Each concept needs a body terminator (coded-from / defined-as /
// definition-is) per CRL grammar. For these fixture concepts —
// CaseFeature-style booleans whose actual CQL lives in the existing
// demo-content-r4 ColorectalCancerCaseFeatures library — the
// `definition is documented.` form is the lightest valid placeholder.
// The emit pipeline only needs the concept name (it becomes the CQL
// identifier in action.condition.expression); the body's semantics
// don't affect FHIR-def emit. Future Homeostasis lane may revise.

concept "Inclusion Criteria":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "Exclusion Criteria":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

// One terminology to exercise Inv 2(b) (Library.relatedArtifact integrity)
// in the closure orchestrator. Plan v3.2 round-4 disposition.
terminology "Coverage Concern VS":
- valueset is `http://example.org/sdh/demo/ValueSet/coverage-concern-vs`.

// Body-only swap from `definition is documented` to `coded from "VS"`
// so this concept now drives a Library.relatedArtifact[depends-on]
// entry on its emitted Library. Other 9 concepts keep their original
// body — they're irrelevant to Inv 2(b) test coverage.
concept "Has Coverage Concern":
- type is Observation.
- coded from "Coverage Concern VS".

concept "No Coverage Concern":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "Has Sedation Concern":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "No Sedation Concern":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "Has Sigmoidoscopy Complications":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "No Sigmoidoscopy Complications":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "Has Colonoscopy Complications":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

concept "No Colonoscopy Complications":
- type is Observation.
- definition is documented.

// ============ Activities ============
// Each `activity` declaration produces TWO FHIR resources:
//   1. cpg-recommendationdefinition PlanDefinition (the wrapping layer
//      that strategies/sub-decisions reference)
//   2. cpg-servicerequestactivity ActivityDefinition (the actual
//      resource the consumer instantiates)

activity "FIT DNA":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

activity "Colonoscopy":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

activity "CT Colonography":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

activity "Sigmoidoscopy":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

// ============ Decisions ============

// Root strategy decision. Produces a cpg-strategydefinition PlanDef
// (type workflow-definition). The single when-then branch (Inclusion)
// delegates to the sub-decision via `use decision`. The example's
// Exclusion branch is intentionally omitted (Drift B per README:
// the example's no-recommendation target has an empty body, which is
// unparseable per CRL grammar `decisionBody : whenBlock+`).

decision "Colorectal Cancer Screening Strategy":
- when "Inclusion Criteria" then use decision "Colorectal Cancer Screening Decision".

// Sub-decision: the actual screening choice tree. Produces a sub-
// decision PlanDef (cpg-publishableplandefinition only; type
// eca-rule). Nested when-then becomes nested action.action[] —
// no leaf `definitionCanonical` until the innermost layer.
//
// The leaves use `recommend activity X` which emits as
// action.definitionCanonical → the wrapping Recommendation PlanDef
// for activity X (NOT directly the ActivityDef — round-2 plan
// review C1 fix).

decision "Colorectal Cancer Screening Decision":
- when "Has Coverage Concern" then recommend activity "FIT DNA".
- when "No Coverage Concern" then:
  - when "Has Sedation Concern" then:
    - when "Has Sigmoidoscopy Complications" then recommend activity "CT Colonography".
    - when "No Sigmoidoscopy Complications" then recommend activity "Sigmoidoscopy".
  - end when
  - when "No Sedation Concern" then:
    - when "Has Colonoscopy Complications" then recommend activity "CT Colonography".
    - when "No Colonoscopy Complications" then recommend activity "Colonoscopy".
  - end when
- end when
